course: dictionary
lesson: 1448
title: One word, more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning is right. «Never touch fireworks, cartridges or flares found on the ground; tell a grown-up, because they may still explode.» Fireworks and flares sit beside cartridges, and things that explode are dangerous, so here a cartridge is the gun case with a bullet and gunpowder inside.
explain: Now look at other clue words. Ink and printer tell you a cartridge is a small container that fits into a pen or machine. Games console tells you it is a plastic case with a game inside. The same word, three different things, each picked out by its context.
explain: Ask yourself: what meaning fits here? Then put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. If "a small ink container" makes no sense in a sentence about explosions, you have picked the wrong meaning. Try another one.
fact: A cartridge is a small container that holds something and fits into a machine or tool.
fact: An ink cartridge fills a pen or printer, and a game cartridge is a plastic case with a game inside, plugged into a games console.
fact: A cartridge can also be the case holding a bullet and gunpowder for a gun, and it is very dangerous.
fact: «Cartridges» found on the ground may still explode, so never touch them; tell a grown-up.
fact: Context clues show you which meaning of a word fits the sentence.
exercise: Pupil says, «I put a new ink cartridge in my pen.» What does cartridge mean here? | A type of fruit | A plastic game case | A gun case holding a bullet | *A small container of ink that fits into a pen
exercise: «Never touch fireworks, cartridges or flares found on the ground.» Why should you not touch them? | They are good for playing games | They are soft and sticky | *They may still explode | They are expensive to buy
exercise: «My game cartridge won't work in the console.» What is a game cartridge? | The case holding a bullet for a gun | A kind of firework | A small container for ink | *A plastic case with a game inside, plugged into a console
test: Which sentence uses cartridge to mean a gun case? | *The bullet and gunpowder were sealed in the cartridge, so it is very dangerous | The printer needed a new cartridge | The game cartridge was plugged into the console
test: «The printer's cartridge is empty, so the page came out pale.» What does cartridge mean? | A plastic case with a game inside | A small bag for carrying coins | *A small container of ink that fits into a printer | The case holding a bullet for a gun
exam: «Water filter cartridges need changing every few months.» What does cartridge mean here? | A gun case holding a bullet and gunpowder | A plastic case with a game inside | *A small container that fits into a machine and holds something | A small bag for carrying coins
